index 0000000..568f972
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/wsh/0043-hw-sparc64-sun4u-add-the-idle-halt-option-on-by-defa.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] hw/sparc64/sun4u: add the idle-halt option, on by default
+
+It halts the CPU while a known guest kernel is idle, see
+target/sparc/sparc64_idle.c. -M sun4u,idle-halt=off lets the idle loop
+spin as before. sun4u has one CPU, so unlike sun4m's options it needs
+no exception for more than one. sun4v doesn't get it: its guests idle
+through hypervisor calls, which QEMU doesn't implement.
+---
