+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] tests/qtest: test the Linux and Solaris 7/8 idle loops on sun4u
+
+sun4u-idle-test gets the Solaris 7/8 layout and three Linux layouts of
+arch_cpu_idle(): 7.3 (be to the sun4v branch, a tail call), 6.1 (be,
+then touch_softlockup_watchdog() and interrupts enabled) and 7.0 (bne
+around the sun4v branch). Solaris 7/8 runs the cases of the other
+layouts. Linux's loop disables interrupts to level 14 round the call of
+arch_cpu_idle() and enables them after it: the CPU must halt there, and
+not with TIF_NEED_RESCHED set, without PSTATE.IE, at level 0 or at level
+15; with a tick every millisecond the tick must wake the CPU at level 14,
+be taken when the loop enables interrupts, and the loop must run far
+fewer rounds than with idle-halt=off. The boot PROM sets up the register
+windows, %g6 and the flags and tlb_type words for it.
+
+Against the binary without the two patches before, the idle and tick
+cases of the new layouts fail.
+---
+ tests/qtest/sun4u-idle-test.c | 213 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
+ 1 file changed, 196 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/tests/qtest/sun4u-idle-test.c b/tests/qtest/sun4u-idle-test.c
